cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its benchmark results, please cite this project
  using the metadata below. Cite the Rousseau source editions separately;
  attribution is provided in SOURCES.md.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
title: "Rousseau: VectorRAG vs. GraphRAG"
authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Killian K."
abstract: >-
  A comparison of vector-based retrieval-augmented generation and GraphRAG
  global search over English translations of Jean-Jacques Rousseau's writings.
  The project includes a 60-question benchmark, saved system answers,
  LLM-as-a-judge evaluations, and analysis of answer preferences and latency.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - GraphRAG
  - vector search
  - Jean-Jacques Rousseau
  - benchmark
  - LLM evaluation
